      "proof_review": {
        "reviewed": true,
        "context_checked": true,
        "method": "Published author proof/core and local context fidelity screening",
        "note": "Complete author Proposition3.6 route is supplied. The field is algebraically closed of characteristic0 and H is the four-dimensional Sweedler Hopf algebra T2(-1). The compared categories are mixed complexes in stable anti-Yetter–Drinfeld contramodules versus mixed anti-Yetter–Drinfeld contramodules, in the precise DG-module sense of2.1–2.3. Full twisted-double relations and sigma grading3.1/3.2, the s=0 comparison3.4 and s=1 algebra/differential are included. The author gives the complete two-term Hochschild-cohomology expression and its center/kernel computation, yielding different dimensions in degree-1. The explicit dual Hopf isomorphism is given with routine verification attributed to prior formulas [16,18], not an omitted new main theorem. Hochschild cohomology invariance for the DG module category is prior background [22]. No semisimple S-square-identity equivalence or general Taft-algebra variant is separately counted."
      },
